    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so permanent. like there is no way to undo what happened and there is no path back to how things were. i look at them all hanging out and it's just... it's like i'm watching a movie of a life i don't even belong to anymore. how am i supposed to just keep pretending i'm part of the world when the world clearly decided i'm not?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that things are permanent is a very heavy weight, but it's important to remember that feelings are not facts. While it feels like you are watching from outside, there are ways to begin rebuilding a sense of belonging, even if it feels impossible right now. Seeking support, whether from friends, family, or a therapist, can help you find a path toward feeling more connected again.",
      "source": "target",
